67. Central Insight

The emerging character is not someone who never detects threat.

The character is someone whose system increasingly does this:

«detect accurately → investigate eagerly → distinguish cue from consequence → map the relationship → map the environment → identify the aim → determine what matters → acquire information → act proportionately → verify reality → update»

The external world becomes rewarding because it continually produces:

- evidence,
- patterns,
- movement,
- information,
- prediction,
- optionality.

The objective is not numbness.

It is:

«high perception with low unnecessary capture.»

And eventually:

«the body learns the same architecture the mind has already discovered.»
